## The layout

```
        Left hand  ANY  Right hand
top :   ; a i o j       v l n r w
home:    h f p e    y    g t c m s
bot :     b x q    u z    k d , . /
```

Full specification — punctuation placement, space thumb, per-letter
fingering guide, statistics, and known trade-offs — in
[`results/LAYOUT.md`](results/LAYOUT.md).

Headline results (Norvig `big.txt`, this repo's model, vs. eight
reference layouts including Colemak-DH, Gallium, Graphite, Canary, and
Sturdy):

| metric (lower/first = better) | this layout | best reference |
|---|---|---|
| trigram cost + balance | **4.388** | 5.576 |
| same-finger bigrams (alt-fingering) | **0.02%** | 0.01–0.20% |
| weak redirects | **0.55%** | 0.28–2.15% |
| ring-pinky scissors | **0.00%** | — |
| same objective on shai-iweb (12-layout table) | **4.4404 (#1)** | 5.6890 |

The #1 rank above also survives 17 of 18 weight-perturbation scenarios of
the scorer itself (the 18th flips by 0.004 and is recovered by local
search) — `results/archive/robustness.txt`. None of the community analyzers can
reproduce these numbers directly; see
[`findings/analyzer_comparison.md`](findings/analyzer_comparison.md) for
why (models differ in fingering, denominator and corpus), and for
percentile-band placement of every metric that tools *can* compare.

## Variants

All keep the same 30-key grid and fingering rules; only letter placement
differs. Full table with scores on all objectives:
[`results/LAYOUT.md`](results/LAYOUT.md#variants).

| variant | when |
|---|---|
| **cfgE** (this repo, installed) | best English — the layout described above |
| cfgG | tie within noise; conventional `;` on the P key |
| cfgE-punct | heavy punctuation/code typing: prices `.` `;` `/` into the objective (kills the `s.` pinky pair, +0.07 English) |
| hybrid-35 / hybrid-80 | Spanish-inclusive typing (see above) |

